@{
    Layout = null;
    ViewData["Title"] = "CryptoSmith X";
}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>CryptoSmith X — multi-venue perpetual market data</title>
<meta name="description" content="Perpetual-market data from four venues, stored as it was seen: every value with its source and time, gaps kept as gaps. Live cross-venue comparison; open source under MIT.">
<meta property="og:title" content="CryptoSmith X">
<meta property="og:description" content="Perpetual-market data from four venues, stored as it was seen: every value with its source and time, gaps kept as gaps. Live cross-venue comparison; open source under MIT.">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:locale" content="en">
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32">
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/ds/styles.css" asp-append-version="true">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/ui-mocks/assets/site.css" asp-append-version="true">
<style>
/* Page-local structure only — site.css is shared with the superseded ui-mocks landing and
   404.html, so it stays untouched; every override needed to drop the auth column and the
   telemetry cards lives here, scoped to this page, reusing the same tokens and classes. */

/* Sign-in moved to /login (item 5): a single text link is all the first screen carries now. */
.topbar{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;padding:14px 24px 0;position:relative;z-index:1}
.topbar a{font:400 13px var(--font-body)}

/* No auth column left, so the two-column grid becomes one. inset:0 matches what the shared
   mobile breakpoint already does for the same reason — the wash no longer has a right rail
   to avoid. */
.split{grid-template-columns:1fr;grid-template-areas:"brand" "data";min-height:0}
.split::before{inset:0}

/* The shared mobile rule hides h1/.prose because the auth column used to own the first
   screen there. That column is gone on every width now, so the headline and body stay. */
@@media (max-width:960px){ h1,.prose{display:block} }

.sub{margin:2px 0 0;font:500 17px/1.4 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-heading)}
.status-line{
  margin:14px 0 0;font:500 10px/1.6 var(--font-mono);letter-spacing:.14em;
  text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--text-faint);
}
.cta-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-top:6px}
.cta-row .btn{width:auto;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:0 22px;text-decoration:none}
.cta-row .link-u{font:500 13px var(--font-body)}
.cta-note{margin:0;font:400 12.5px/1.5 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-muted)}

/* Three plain blocks, same card shell the telemetry tiles used — no icons, no glow, just a
   status word and a paragraph each. */
.blocks{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}
.blocks .card{padding:14px}
.blocks .card__head{padding:0 0 10px;border-bottom:0}
.blocks .card p{margin:0;font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-body)}
a.block-link{display:block;color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
a.block-link:hover .card{border-color:var(--border-strong)}
@@media (max-width:960px){ .blocks{grid-template-columns:1fr} }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="shell">
  <div class="rule"></div>
  <div class="topbar"><a class="link-u" href="/login">Sign in</a></div>

  <div class="split">

    <!-- ─── знак и заголовок ─── -->
    <section class="pane pane--brand">
      <div class="brand">
        <img class="brand-lockup"
             src="/ds/assets/cryptosmith-lockup-descriptor.svg"
             width="267" height="48"
             alt="CryptoSmith X — market data, multi-venue">
      </div>

      <h1>CryptoSmith X</h1>
      <p class="sub">Market data that remembers how it looked at the time.</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>Perpetual-market data from four venues, stored the way it was seen: every value with
           its source and the time it arrived, gaps kept as gaps, nothing reconstructed
           afterwards.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="status-line">Collecting since 1 September 2026 · Kraken Futures · WEEX · Hyperliquid · Binance USD-M</p>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/arena/BTC/USD">See a pair across venues</a>
        <a class="link-u" href="https://github.com/blyn-ai/CryptoSmith-X">GitHub · MIT</a>
      </div>
      <p class="cta-note">A free live API and a Base MCP plugin are in preparation. Avantis is the next venue.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── studio / arena / agent ─── -->
    <section class="pane pane--data">
      <div class="cards blocks">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head"><span>Studio</span><span class="meta">running</span></div>
          <p>Ticker, funding, open interest, order-book depth by band and 1-minute candles with
             derived timeframes, about 2,000 instruments across four venues. Instruments are
             discovered automatically and keep their dates. Trades are next; nothing is backfilled
             silently.</p>
        </div>

        <a class="block-link" href="/arena">
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card__head"><span>Arena</span><span class="meta">running</span></div>
            <p>One instrument, every venue that quotes it, each figure carrying the age of the
               call that wrote it.</p>
          </div>
        </a>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head"><span>Agent</span><span class="meta">prototype</span></div>
          <p>Each bot is its own container against one exchange account: its own keys, its own
             journal. Two instances of the previous generation trade the company's own funds on
             this data — that is how we test it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <footer>
    <p>MB BlynAI is not a financial institution, an investment manager or a provider of financial services.
       <button type="button" class="linkish" id="openLegal">Read more</button></p>
    <p class="copy">blynai.eu · © 2026 MB „BlynAI“</p>
  </footer>
</div>

<dialog class="modal" id="legal" aria-labelledby="legalTitle">
  <button class="modal__close" type="button" id="closeLegal" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
  <div class="modal__in">
    <h2 id="legalTitle">MB BlynAI</h2>
    <p>MB BlynAI is not a financial institution, an investment manager or a provider of financial
       services. The company gives no investment advice, does not accept or hold third-party money
       or crypto assets, and does not operate third-party exchange accounts. It trades its own
       funds only; published results are research data, not an offer or a forecast.</p>

    <h3>Trading own funds</h3>
    <p>The software runs as two independent instances — LUKAS and BYKO. Same code, separate
       accounts, separate journals.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>only the company's and its members' funds are traded;</li>
      <li>each instance runs on its own exchange account with its own API keys;</li>
      <li>strategy, risk limits and parameters are set by the members themselves;</li>
      <li>there are no client funds, and there will be none.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>No third-party assets</h3>
    <p>The company:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>does not accept or hold third-party money or crypto assets;</li>
      <li>does not operate third-party exchange accounts;</li>
      <li>holds no API permissions that would let it dispose of anyone else's funds, and asks for none;</li>
      <li>accepts no investments and gives no individual investment advice.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Published results</h3>
    <p>Published figures are historical research data for a specific instance and a specific
       period. They do not guarantee future results and are not an offer, a forecast or individual
       investment advice. Failed experiments are published the same as successful ones.</p>

    <h3>Company status</h3>
    <p>MB BlynAI is a small partnership registered in the Republic of Lithuania. Members — Lukas
       Peciukonis and Denisas Bykovas. Director — Lukas Peciukonis. Contact —
       <a href="mailto:info@@blynai.eu">info@@blynai.eu</a>.</p>
  </div>
</dialog>

<script>
(function () {
  'use strict';
  var legal = document.getElementById('legal');
  document.getElementById('openLegal').addEventListener('click', function () { legal.showModal(); });
  document.getElementById('closeLegal').addEventListener('click', function () { legal.close(); });
  legal.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target === legal) legal.close(); });
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
